understanding as well as these records; the last execution is not the default next task.\",\n    \"execution_capacity\": {\n      \"available\": true,\n      \"timeout_ceiling_seconds\": 1200.0,\n      \"note\": \"Capacity is not a runtime estimate. Include construction/review time; source work remains useful if a test will not fit.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"citation_scope\": \"Result citations locate current and historical uses; an absent citation is not a task to clear. One applicable receipt can support multiple questions without a dedicated execution for each.\",\n  \"current\": {},\n  \"validation\": {\n    \"command\": [\n      \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python\",\n      \"-I\",\n      \"-B\",\n      \"-c\",\n      \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\",\n      \"validate\",\n      \"--run\",\n      \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_21-49-09-omnipaxos-real-run\",\n      \"--submission\"\n    ],\n    \"read_only_paths\": [\n      \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src\",\n      \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages\",\n      \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin\",\n      \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/pyvenv.cfg\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"tools\": {\n    \"agent\": \"codex-cli 0.162.0-alpha.17.2\",\n    \"implementation\": \"rustc 1.94.1 (e408947bf 2026-03-25)\\nbinary: rustc\\ncommit-hash: e408947bfd200af42db322daf0fadfe7e26d3bd1\\ncommit-date: 2026-03-25\\nhost: x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\\nrelease: 1.94.1\\nLLVM version: 21.1.8\"\n  },\n  \"build_inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"record\": \"build-inputs/targets/omnipaxos/assurance_generated/basis.json\",\n      \"manifest\": \"omnipaxos/Cargo.toml\",\n      \"test_target\": \"assurance_generated\",\n      \"resolved_features\": [\n        \"async_runtime\",\n        \"default\",\n        \"logging\",\n        \"macros\",\n        \"omnipaxos_macros\",\n        \"serde\",\n        \"slog\",\n        \"slog-async\",\n        \"slog-term\"\n      ],\n      \"feature_evidence\": \"metadata resolution; selected test compilation is recorded separately\",\n      \"compilations\": [],\n      \"status\": \"inputs_fixed\",\n      \"latest_preparation\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"cargo\",\n    \"harness_kind\": \"rust_test\",\n    \"harness_filename\": \"omnipaxos/tests/assurance_generated.rs\",\n    \"default_execution_package\": \"./omnipaxos\",\n    \"instructions\": \"Write Rust #[test] integration tests using the captured crate's public API and existing dependencies. The controller fixes the workspace lock and tools; build reuse is specific to a manifest, integration test target and saved build basis. Switching crates may require a first heavy dependency build. Consult research.json build_inputs for preparation evidence and current seed availability; unlisted targets are not known to be prepared, and available seeds still require execution-time validation. Only the generated test target runs, serially with --nocapture and --locked --offline. Optional test_names selects exact full test names; omission runs the whole generated target. Unselected code still compiles. Emit complete CA_EVENT JSON lines. Helpers are workspace-relative; never replace manifests, locks, build scripts or Cargo configuration. No extra feature flags are added; original dev-dependencies can enable additional features. Actual compiler-artifact records describe reuse; declaration syntax does not establish active cfg branches or private-state reachability.\",\n    \"network\": \"Agent shell networking is disabled. Isolated target execution may communicate only inside its private network namespace.\",\n    \"support_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_21-49-09-omnipaxos-real-run/target-support\"\n  },\n  \"example\": {\n    \"rationale\": \"Investigate a sourced local uncertainty\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"source\",\n        \"file\": \"REPLACE_WITH_CAPTURED_FILE\",\n        \"start_line\": 1,\n        \"end_line\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"investigations\": [\n      {\n        \"ref\": \"@question\",\n        \"question\": \"Which applicable caller condition establishes this result?\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"source\"\n        ],\n        \"discriminator\": \"Trace the actual producer and the enclosing protection\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"optional_experiment\": {\n    \"investigation_id\": \"@question\",\n    \"harness_path\": \"omnipaxos/tests/assurance_generated.rs\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"source\"\n    ],\n    \"scope\": {\n      \"description\": \"Observe the sourced local behavior\"\n    },\n    \"prefix\": \"Describe actual initialization and producer calls in the draft harness, including supplied state\"\n  },\n  \"costs\": {\n    \"agent_calls\": 1,\n    \"target_executions\": 0,\n    \"process_seconds\": 0,\n    \"action_seconds\": 0,\n    \"unrecorded_action_ids\": [],\n    \"elapsed_seconds\": 4.984167327999785\n  }\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
